        rules: {
          objective: "Score points by winning tricks and capturing 'count' tiles. Be the first team to reach 500 points.",
          gameplay: "1. Bidding: Starts left of dealer. Bids range from 60 to 88 (jumping in increments of 2). Multiples of 88 (176, 264, etc.) are used for aggressive hands.\n2. The Kitty: The high bidder takes the 2 kitty tiles and discards 2 tiles of their choice (cannot discard count tiles into the kitty).\n3. Play: Winner of the bid leads the first tile and names trumps (a specific suit or 'No Trumps').\n4. Identical Tiles: Since there are two sets, if two identical tiles are played in one trick, the FIRST one played wins.",
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit (follow the high end of the tile led).',
            'Winning bidder reveals their trump choice AFTER exchanging with the kitty.',
            'The kitty contains no points unless specifically allowed by house rules.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'In a 6-player game, information is highly fragmented. Trust your teammates to help clear suits you are weak in.',
          intermediate: "The Duplicate Rule: Use the 'First One Wins' rule to your advantage. If you know the other set's Ace is still in play, play yours early to gain the lead on tie-breaks.",
          advanced: "Kitty Management: Discard tiles into the kitty that clarify your 'No Trump' leads. If you can void a suit by discarding into the kitty, you can trump in earlier.",
          tips: [
            'Bidding is conservative at the start; only jump above 60 if you have a strong set of doubles.',
            "With 6 players, 'No Trump' bids are significantly riskier than in 4-player Texas 42.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
